  "verbalization": "Hex-3-en-1-yl 2-methylbut-2-enoate is implicated in the biological activity of DMS-273 through a series of target relationships, all pointing to Caspase-5 as a central mediator. The evidence suggests that this compound acts as a target for multiple compounds, including 5-Oxobrucine and 5-(2-Thienylethynyl)-2-thiophenemethanol, which in turn target DMS-273. These pathways highlight a potential mechanism by which Hex-3-en-1-yl 2-methylbut-2-enoate influences DMS-273, likely through the activation of Caspase-5. The presence of multiple distinct compounds sharing the same target relationship underscores the possibility of a broader biological role for Caspase-5 in the context of DMS-273. The integration of these findings suggests that the compound may exert its effects via a common pathway involving Caspase-5, potentially with varying modulatory properties depending on the specific ligand.",
